cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite the essay and the code as below."
title: "Every line is a loop: what would a maximally plausible periodic table for biology look like?"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Titterton
    given-names: Katherine
    affiliation: Macrofluidics
repository-code: "https://github.com/kat-titter/every-line-is-a-loop"
url: "https://kat-titter.github.io/every-line-is-a-loop/every-line-is-a-loop.html"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - feedback loops
  - systems biology
  - BioModels
  - periodic table
  - SBML
abstract: >-
  An essay proposing a periodic table of feedback circuits in cells (loops, braking loops, running totals) and the
  code that tests it: a census of the 640 curated models of BioModels release 31 and a hold-out of 435 models curated
  since. One command rebuilds every number in the essay from the raw downloads.
references:
